  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a binary string `s`, output *the **smallest** number of character swaps to make it **alternating**, or* `-1` *if it is impossible.*\n\nThe string is called **alternating** if no two adjacent characters are equal. As an example, the strings `\"010\"` and `\"1010\"` are alternating, while the string `\"0100\"` is not.\n\nAny two characters may be swapped, even if they are **not adjacent**.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"111000\"\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: Swap positions 1 and 4: \"111000\" -> \"101010\"\nThe string is now alternating.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"010\"\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: The string is already alternating, no swaps are needed.\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"1110\"\nOutput: -1\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 1000`\n* `s[i]` is either `'0'` or `'1'`.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
